/-
# Certificate for the §29 and §31 Young-channel weights

`H4VertexEnergy.lean` proves the algebra of the summed weights `wInit`, `wFinal`, and
`BBorWeightTrace.lean` the bare β_Bor split, but the state weights themselves
(`Σ_λ q^{c(λ)} P_λ`, with `P_λ` the Lagrange idempotents of the full twist) were exact sympy
computations only (energy-map audit §29, §31 D2). This file certifies them in Lean.

All matrices act on the weight-zero space of `V^{⊗4}`, basis `uudd, udud, uddu, duud, dudu, dduu`,
with `h = q - q⁻¹`. Generated matrices are sympy output, checked here entry by entry.

* `D_eq` … `F3_eq`: `D = σ₁σ₂σ₃`, its square, the full twist `F = D⁴`, `F²`, `F³`.
* `F_minpoly`: `(F - q¹²)(F - q⁴)(F - 1) = 0`, so the three Lagrange polynomials are
  orthogonal idempotents summing to `1`.
* `W_eq`: `W = Σ_λ q^{c(λ)} P_λ` with `c = 6, 2, 0` on `(4), (3,1), (2,2)`.
* `W_init_sum`, `W_final_sum`: its diagonal sums over the initial and final sets are the
  `wInit`, `wFinal` of `H4VertexEnergy` (§29).
* `D2_init_sum`, `D2_final_sum`: the β_Bor-dressed sums of §31 D2.
-/
import QOU.QBeta.H4VertexEnergy
import QOU.QBeta.BBorWeightTrace

namespace QOU.QBeta.H4YoungChannelCert

open QOU.QBeta.H4VertexEnergy QOU.QBeta.BBorWeightTrace

